.1-rc. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and why it was promoted even though the staging RC was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 45090, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017WBpKEhsWL8UyQmHS4BP2w", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_timeout"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 45090, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017WBpKEhsWL8UyQmHS4BP2w", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 48791, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. I rolled it back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also lists one follow-up: finding out why v2.3.1 failed and why it reached production when its staging test build (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy.\n\nNo approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012MdG1NVoWt5gAan3cH4tYm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RazJaYRLba9YbvxuBRUq46", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SkoXhBecJuDThjxmGEDSsz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WCG1Hjw3KH5zKc3xanfjH6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CfseN39pvs837MMvuUbWv6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017WBpKEhsWL8UyQmHS4BP2w", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks with an error rate of 18% in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The same build was also unhealthy in staging as v2.3.1-rc. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and why it was promoted even though the staging RC was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. I rolled it back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also lists one follow-up: finding out why v2.3.1 failed and why it reached production when its staging test build (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy.\n\nNo approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}